MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_001: Oh, what a commotion.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_002: Commander Bonaventure? Did you call for me?
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_003: I have some gifts for you. They are from the maidens\nyou saw outside.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_004: Pressed flowers, perfumes, wine...\nA lavish assortment.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_005: This is embarrassing. I told them not to do all this\nwhen we dined together.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_006: I was aware that you pass your breaks by spending\ntime with several maidens.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_007: I cannot fault a boy of your age for such behavior.\nBut a warrior of Saramis should be more temperate.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_008: I appreciate the word of warning, but it's not\nserious with any of them.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_009: We have dinner, we chat, and then we part ways\nbefore nightfall.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_010: Hrm. Is this true?
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_011: We don't get intimate. Ask any of them.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_012: No need. As I said, I do not fault you in this.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_013: Thank you, sir. I apologize for any trouble I've\ncaused you.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_014: Though now I am worried in the other direction.\nYou may be passing up a lifelong companion.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_015: To my eye, at least a few of those maidens would\nbe happy to play the part.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_016: You think so? Be that as it may, I'm not interested.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_017: I've already decided not to get married until I can\nsurpass my late father.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_018: You mean Kleitos?
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_019: Yes. He left big shoes for me to fill.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_020: He was a fearless warrior, yet also a kindhearted\nhusband who cherished my mother.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_021: Ah, yes. Your father and mother were perfectly\nmatched. Theirs was a model union.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_022: I dream of building a family like that one day.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_023: But first, I must become the kind of man my\nfuture wife can be proud of!
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_024: Mm. You are still young, but with effort and\npatience, you may achieve it.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_025: Yes, sir! Now, I should be going.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_C_026: Ah, Kleitos. When I remember your final moments...\nAhhh...
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_001: Hnnng... Ngaaah!
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_002: Oh! Lysander!
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_003: Commander Bonaventure?! Hang in there!
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_004: Augh!
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_005: Are you alright, Commander?
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_006: Ah... Lysander. I am glad you are unharmed.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_007: Why would you put yourself in harm's way for me?
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_008: You are the Living Archive of Saramis. Your life is\nfar more valuable than mine!
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_009: I...suppose that is true. For Her Majesty's sake,\nI must not be eager to throw my life away.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_010: But I could not stand by and watch the son of my\nold friend Kleitos make the same mistake he did.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_011: How dare you speak of him that way?!
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_012: He died an honorable death, sacrificing himself for\nhis comrades during the War of Grania.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_013: That's how a fearless warrior ought to be!\nThere is no higher—
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_014: Enough!
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_015: Huh?
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_016: I will hear no more. Yes, there was honor in what\nhe did.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_017: But when I see you, I recall his eyes as death\ncame upon him.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_018: That's right... Weren't you one of the lucky ones who\ncame home alive from the War of Grania?
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_019: Indeed. Among the lives your father saved was mine.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_020: He used his sword to lop off his ponytail and tossed\nthe bundle to me.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_021: "See that my wife gets this," he said. And then...
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_022: My mother later gave that hair to me as a memento.\nI didn't know I had you to thank.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_023: Do not thank me for anything. I failed to recover\nthe rest of him.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_024: They say you never forget anything, Commander.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_025: I hope you won't take this the wrong way, but try\nto make an exception in this case.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_026: My father would not have wished this torment\non you.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_027: Even if my memory were not perfect, those events\nwould haunt me to my dying day.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_028: Then might you remember me in my father's place?
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_029: You?
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_030: Yes. I want to fight shoulder to shoulder with you,\nas my own man.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_B_031: Oh! Ahhh.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_001: Hraaagh!
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_002: Ah, you are training hard, Lysander. I have never\nseen you pull that one off.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_003: Thank you! But I still have room to improve.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_004: I will redouble my efforts. For Saramis, and to\nsurpass my father!
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_005: Oho. I expect nothing less.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_006: That said, I have something I wish to discuss.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_007: With me? Is it a message from Her Majesty?
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_008: No. It is a personal matter.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_009: Are you aware that I am divorced with no children\nof my own?
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_010: Yes. My uncle has mentioned as much.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_011: Your uncle Kumos—our country's chancellor—has\noften put a question to me.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_012: "What will become of your vast estate when the\ntime comes, Bonaventure Satornio?"
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_013: Er...
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_014: To that end, I propose to adopt you.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_015: Huh? You— What?!
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_016: Not right now, of course. We can begin proceedings\nonce things settle down.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_017: Now wait a moment—I appreciate the offer, but...
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_018: You would find in me a discreet father. I would never\nmeddle in matters such as your marriage.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_019: I simply wish to have a fine young man like yourself\nas an heir. That is all I ask.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_020: I'm...honored, but I would need to talk it over with\nmy uncle first.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_021: He raised me, you know, after I left home when\nI could no longer stand my stepfather.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_022: Ah, but I knew that one with a heart so sincere\nwould raise just such an objection.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_023: And so I took the liberty of approaching Kumos\nfirst to seek his permission.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_024: Things have already gone that far?! Was my uncle\nopen to the idea?
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_025: If only! He was adamantly opposed to it.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_026: He sent his fastest messenger, in fact, to tell me,\n"I could never surrender my darling nephew!"
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_027: He sent a runner just for that?! Is this a joke?
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_028: He did what he felt the gravity of the situation\ndemanded. Though I will not yield either.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_029: You might say that Kumos and I are locked in a\ntug-of-war over you.
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_030: Who knows? It may escalate into open conflict, as if\nyou were a prize to be won! Hahaha!
MID_SE_Bon_Lys_A_031: This has to be a joke...right?